{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200/resnet50, avgpool, weighted → 0.678 acc, 5.90 GPU-h), evidence is very sparse. The most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality is actually contributing signal or adding noise. Config_002 is the direct RNA-only ablation of config_001 (same scvi_n200 encoder, same multiprofile/avgpool setup, no image branch), so any accuracy difference isolates the value of the image modality and the fusion step. If RNA-only matches or exceeds 0.678, the fusion is not helping and we should pivot to improving the RNA pipeline or trying different encoders; if it falls well below, multimodal is confirmed as the right direction and we can invest remaining budget in stronger image encoders (ViT-L) or better aggregation (transformer). This experiment is also the cheapest multimodal-related test (~3–4 GPU-h, no image encoder), preserving budget for later exploitation. It is the single highest-information, lowest-cost next step under the 8-experiment remainder."
}

